From 348b448076ab563d52cce962f465b6b200a9785b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:04:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pick): the pick door takes an edge pick whose stitched
 ring has no area

A plain click on a vertical edge selected nothing, and the first
Ctrl+click on an edge under the first one added nothing: the pocket
family's flat-area door refused the selection, because the stitcher
welds open runs whose ends meet seen from above into a ring with no
area. The door now lets such a stitched collapse in (an edge pick in
progress); Generate keeps the refusal and the Geometry page still says
it. A wall face or a closed chain on a wall is refused as before.

Pinned by pick_doors::edge_picks_that_meet_only_from_above_pass_the_pick_door
and the ui frame tests in egui_app::tests::first_ctrl_click.

Fixes #1726

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
